# (more visible enemy champions than allies within 4 tiles). It keeps walking to tribute instead.
# Everything else from v1 is unchanged.
# v1: v7-zerogem + ability filtering. Heals and shields are never cast at enemies or camps. Damage,
# stun and AoE abilities go on fight targets, and a self shield goes up below 60% health in a fight.
# v7-zerogem: v7 + fixes for the three maps where a v7 mirror tributes nothing (docs/ZERO_GEM_MAPS.md):
# no fighting enemies on their own spawn, fight a camp that is the only way to an altar, and go
# for monoliths when nothing is tributed by round 300.
# v7: v5d-fs2 + idle fix: when standing on a dead camp of an uncleared group, walk to the nearest
# living camp instead of idling.
# v5d-fs2 [hybrid line]: v5d plus Treasure/Jungle shards; tribute at >= 10 gems, when hurt, or after round 1500.
# v5d: v5 with a fixed draft order.
# v5: v4 attacking the weakest enemy in range (focus fire) instead of the first.
# v4: v3 + altar fixes: never freeze when every altar is locked, and prefer altars out of monolith reach.
# v3: retreat toward spawn below 30% health while in_danger() and recall only once clear; hold on a
# camp tile only when its group is capturable; skip monoliths and golems.
# Based on fs-1: split strength/health shards, heal on spawn, retreat at 50% health when carrying gems,
# hold on a cleared camp spawn to capture, one camps_visible() query per turn.

# attack-type abilities only (no heals or shields) on a fight target
def fight_unit(u):
    if ability_ready(0) and (slot_is_damage(0) or slot_is_stun(0) or slot_is_aoe(0)):
